<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- Default grants of joan's runtime permissions.

     privapp-permissions (org.joan.ims.xml) cannot do this. That file
     allowlists signature|privileged permissions; a dangerous runtime
     permission is neither granted by an entry there nor required to have
     one.

     WHEN THIS APPLIES. PackageManagerService.systemReady() runs
     DefaultPermissionGrantPolicy.grantDefaultPermissions() for a user
     whenever the fingerprint recorded at the last grant differs from
     Build.FINGERPRINT: the first boot of a fresh install, and the first
     boot after every ROM update. Exceptions are granted with
     whitelistRestrictedPermissions=true, so the hard-restricted
     background location permission is covered as well.

     So flash the joan zip in the same recovery session as the ROM,
     after a clean install or after each ROM update (which has to be
     followed by re-flashing joan anyway), and the microphone and
     location are granted on the next boot with no taps and no adb.

     Flashing joan alone onto a ROM that has already booted does NOT
     change the fingerprint, so this file waits for the next ROM update.
     That case was measured: alpha63 shipped this file and the tester's
     row still read pani_cell=no-permission. For it, open "joan IMS" from
     the launcher once (JoanPermissionActivity), or over adb with no root:

       adb shell pm grant org.joan.ims android.permission.RECORD_AUDIO
       adb shell pm grant org.joan.ims android.permission.ACCESS_FINE_LOCATION
       adb shell pm grant org.joan.ims android.permission.ACCESS_COARSE_LOCATION
       adb shell pm grant org.joan.ims android.permission.ACCESS_BACKGROUND_LOCATION

     scripts/grant-permissions.sh runs exactly those.

     What each is for:
       RECORD_AUDIO   the uplink. Without it AudioRecord opens and returns
                      digital silence: the far end hears nothing.
       location       getAllCellInfo, so P-Access-Network-Info can carry
                      utran-cell-id-3gpp (TS 24.229 7.2A.4). Nothing else.
                      BACKGROUND because an ImsService has no UI and is
                      always a background process.

     fixed="false" on all of them, so every grant can be revoked in
     Settings. A revoked location grant costs one header parameter; a
     revoked microphone costs the uplink, and the trace says so
     (media capture record_audio=DENIED).

     NOT here: LOCATION_BYPASS, which is signature|privileged and granted
     by the privapp allowlist instead. -->
<exceptions>
    <exception package="org.joan.ims">
        <permission name="android.permission.RECORD_AUDIO" fixed="false"/>
        <permission name="android.permission.ACCESS_COARSE_LOCATION" fixed="false"/>
        <permission name="android.permission.ACCESS_FINE_LOCATION" fixed="false"/>
        <permission name="android.permission.ACCESS_BACKGROUND_LOCATION" fixed="false"/>
    </exception>
</exceptions>
